      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh.... I suppose that makes sense.\n\nThe short answer is that those should be temporary, so probably not worth the hassle?  If this CL is sub-optimal we can revert it in couple of days.\n\nThe long answer is that I added couple of RBE invocations in ART.  Those should be rare and only used in ART-specific builds.  However, there is a risk that I am wrong, and the RBE invocations prove either more common, or more expensive than I expect, which has potential to overload RBE, and thus take it down for all of Android.\n\nSo until the new RBE invocations prove themselves the RBE team asked for client-side environment kill-switch to control the new requests (since the server-side does not have capability to deny any overloading requests).  \n\nWe can remove the environment variables again in couple of days if nothing goes wrong.",
